    <string name="regles_titre">Game rules</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_chiffres_titre">Numbers mode</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_chiffres_texte">6 numbers are drawn (from 1 to 10 in double copies, and 25/50/75/100 in single copies), along with a target to reach. Build your calculation step by step, calculator-style: touch a first number, an operator, then a second number — the result replaces the two numbers used and can be reused. The \"Undo\" and \"Clear\" buttons let you go back. The last result obtained is your proposal: submit as soon as you\'re ready, or let the clock run out if there is one.</string>
    <string name="regles_comptage_points_titre">Scoring</string>
    <string name="regles_chiffres_points_emile_nestor">Assez facile, Émile and Ça va encore, Nestor: 10 points if the count is exact, 5 points for any non-exact proposal.</string>
    <string name="regles_chiffres_points_monique_mathieu">Ça se complique, Monique and Là c\'est sérieux, Mathieu: 10 points if the count is exact, 7 points for a close count (gap of at most 100 from the target), 0 points beyond that.</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_lettres_titre">Letters mode</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_lettres_texte">Choose the number of vowels you want (2, 3, 4 or 5), then all 10 letters are drawn at once. Build your word by touching the letters in the order you want (each drawn letter can only be used once); the \"Undo\" and \"Clear\" buttons let you go back. Find the longest word possible with these letters, before the clock runs out if there is one.</string>
    <string name="regles_lettres_points_emile_nestor">Assez facile, Émile and Ça va encore, Nestor: 5 points for a word of 2 to 4 letters, 10 points from 5 letters up.</string>
    <string name="regles_lettres_points_monique_mathieu">Ça se complique, Monique and Là c\'est sérieux, Mathieu: the score equals the number of letters in the validated word.</string>
    <string name="regles_mots_acceptes_titre">Accepted words</string>
    <string name="regles_mots_acceptes_texte">The built-in dictionary excludes proper nouns, acronyms/abbreviations, and purely conjugated verb forms: only the infinitive and present/past participles remain accepted.</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_entrainement_titre">Training mode</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_entrainement_texte">No time limit or round limit: choose a level (numbers or letters) and play as many rounds as you want, at your own pace. To stop, use the back arrow at the top of the screen; the session is then saved to your statistics.</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_partie_solo_titre">Solo game mode</string>
    <string name="regles_partie_solo_intro">Only one choice to make: the level, applied to numbers and letters rounds, played alternately. The clock duration and number of rounds are fixed per level:</string>
    <string name="regles_partie_solo_emile">Assez facile, Émile (2 rounds per mode) — Numbers: target ≤ 100, addition and subtraction only, solution guaranteed, 120s. Letters: no letters excluded, 110s.</string>
    <string name="regles_partie_solo_nestor">Ça va encore, Nestor (3 rounds per mode) — Numbers: target ≤ 100, all 4 operations, solution guaranteed, 100s. Letters: no letters excluded, 90s.</string>
    <string name="regles_partie_solo_monique">Ça se complique, Monique (4 rounds per mode) — Numbers: target ≤ 500, all 4 operations, no solution guarantee, 60s. Letters: no letters excluded, 50s.</string>
    <string name="regles_partie_solo_mathieu">Là c\'est sérieux, Mathieu (5 rounds per mode) — Numbers: target between 100 and 999, no solution guarantee, 45s. Letters: no letters excluded, 40s.</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_partie_duo_titre">Duo game mode</string>
    <string name="regles_partie_duo_intro">Two players on the same phone, taking turns: after choosing the opponent, the level (as in solo) and the scoring mode, each round is played by both players on exactly the same draw (same numbers and target in numbers mode, same letters in letters mode). The starting player changes every round, so the choice of number of vowels doesn\'t always fall to the same person:</string>
    <string name="regles_partie_duo_mode_duo">Duo: each player keeps their own score on every round, just like solo.</string>
    <string name="regles_partie_duo_mode_confrontation">Head-to-head: on every round, only the player closest to the target (or with the longest word) scores points; in case of a tie, both keep them.</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_defi_serie_titre">Streak challenge mode</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_serie_intro">Choose a mode (numbers or letters) and a level, then chain rounds to line up as many successes in a row as possible, with the same clock as in a solo game for that level. A success is an exact count in numbers, or a valid word of at least a minimum length in letters:</string>
    <string name="regles_seuil_emile">Émile: 4 letters</string>
    <string name="regles_seuil_nestor">Nestor: 5 letters</string>
    <string name="regles_seuil_monique">Monique: 6 letters</string>
    <string name="regles_seuil_mathieu">Mathieu: 7 letters</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_serie_chiffres_note">In numbers, an exact solution is always guaranteed, even on Monique and Mathieu: the challenge only stops on a mistake or when time runs out. The streak obtained is saved to your statistics.</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_defi_chrono_titre">Timed challenge mode</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_chrono_intro">Same principle as the streak challenge, but against the clock: an overall time budget is set per level:</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_chrono_budget_emile">Émile: 2 minutes</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_chrono_budget_nestor">Nestor: 3 minutes</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_chrono_budget_monique">Monique: 4 minutes</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_chrono_budget_mathieu">Mathieu: 5 minutes</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_chrono_seuil_intro">A success is an exact count in numbers, or a valid word of at least a minimum length in letters (the same as in the streak challenge):</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_chrono_detail">The goal is to line up as many successes as possible before time runs out. Unlike the streak challenge, a mistake doesn\'t end the challenge: it simply counts as zero, and the next round starts right away with the remaining time. The current round can be cut off partway through if time runs out. The rules of the chosen level apply normally (target and operations in numbers, excluded letters in letters mode, with no forced solution guarantee on Monique and Mathieu). The number of successes obtained is saved to your statistics.</string>
    <string name="regles_mode_defi_quotidien_titre">Daily challenge mode</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_quotidien_texte1">A streak or timed challenge, in numbers or letters, is drawn at random each day with a goal to reach (number of successes, or successes in a row depending on the type drawn); the draw is the same all day, but different from one profile to another. The level remains free: it alone determines the difficulty of reaching the goal.</string>
    <string name="regles_defi_quotidien_texte2">Once the day\'s goal is reached, the challenge locks until the next day; if you fail before reaching it, you can retry the same day. Two trophies reward a streak of consecutive successful days (7 and 30 days).</string>

